{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/850","id":4129389355,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU872IXsr","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/850","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/850.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/850.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/850","number":850,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Generalize grounded tool actions across local search and research","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Generalizes the three reported journeys into one meanings-driven grounded-action recipe: recognize typed scope, take the smallest observable action, verify its result, widen only when justified, and synthesize scoped evidence.\n- Makes explicit local Desktop/Home/current-directory scope dominate generic search verbs across English, Russian, Hindi, and Chinese.\n- Replaces the single compound local `find` with a stateful exact-name → stable-substring → bounded-inventory ladder, one command per step, with type checks, empty-result handling, discrepancy reporting, and honest scope limits.\n- Resolves definition follow-ups against only their antecedent, researches unresolved definition requests without exposing capability menus, and decomposes comparisons into independent searches for both operands.\n- Makes report creation atomic through `formal-ai context report`, including private temporary-file handling and localized report prompts.\n- Handles transport-wrapped CLI prompts without treating the entire quoted request as a filename, and verifies hard-wrapped final answers from the real OpenCode TUI.\n- Adds a reusable data/meta recipe, Rust/JavaScript parity coverage, a changelog fragment, deterministic fixtures, and real Agent CLI evidence.\n\n## Measured outcome\n\nThe committed 24-node task ladder decomposes #838, #827, and #826 through four levels. The pre-change `v0.303.0` baseline passed **8/24**.\n\nThe release binary on this branch passes **24/24**:\n\n```text\nL1: 3/3\nL2: 6/6\nL3: 7/7\nL4: 8/8\n\n#838 local discovery: 10/10\n#827 definition/follow-up: 7/7\n#826 comparison/report: 7/7\n```\n\nThe exact reported fixture contains `Desktop/Archive/hive-control-center/` beside the PEM decoy `hive-mind-bot.2025-12-26.private-key.pem`. The journey first observes that the requested exact folder name is absent, widens once, verifies the directory, and reports both the discovered path and name mismatch without treating the PEM file as the answer.\n\nThe complete procedure, fixture, residual uncertainty, and evidence are preserved in the [issue #840 case study](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-840-6654ade0a597/docs/case-studies/issue-840).\n\n## Real client verification\n\nFresh release-mode runs pass all three journeys through the real Agent CLI, while local discovery also passes through OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, and the frame-captured OpenCode TUI:\n\n- local search: exact observation → evidence-driven widen → verified final answer;\n- definition follow-up: 1 search, 3 source fetches, final synthesis without source furniture;\n- comparison: 2 independent searches, then a two-sided synthesis.\n\nThe harness and deterministic MCP fixture are in [`experiments/agent_cli_e2e/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-840-6654ade0a597/experiments/agent_cli_e2e). Native client streams, server traces, and dialog logs are retained in the [case-study evidence](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-840-6654ade0a597/docs/case-studies/issue-840/agent-cli-e2e).\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\n```text\ncargo test --test integration -- --test-threads=1\ncargo test --test unit -- --test-threads=4\ncargo test --test issue_712\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\ncargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\ncargo doc --no-deps\nsh src/web/wasm-worker/build.sh\nbun run build:web\nrust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs\nrust-script scripts/check-associative-terminology.rs\nrust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs\nrust-script scripts/check-worker-line-budget.rs\n```\n\nResults on the final product commit:\n\n- integration: **193 passed, 0 failed**;\n- unit: **2,026 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored by existing declarations**;\n- #712 capability-routing compatibility: **7 passed, 0 failed**;\n- task ladder: **24/24**;\n- all three real Agent CLI journeys and all local-search client/TUI variants: passed;\n- transport-wrapped prompt and hard-wrapped TUI regressions: passed;\n- formatting, Clippy, docs, WASM, web bundle, workflow lint, and repository policy checks: passed.\n\nThe serialized integration command avoids this repository's known loopback-port contention under parallel host load; the same affected tests pass under serialization.\n\n## Formal AI self-authorship evidence\n\nThe five smallest reviewed leaves are enumerated in [`self-hosting/decomposition.lino`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-840-6654ade0a597/docs/case-studies/issue-840/self-hosting/decomposition.lino). Formal AI authored and verified one of those five leaves, satisfying the requested **20%** threshold.\n\nSession `ses_069af4151ffep7T8HoP6ObsuBY` produced the grounded-action invariant. The raw Agent stream, server trace, authored artifact, and matching commit trailers are preserved under [`self-hosting/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-840-6654ade0a597/docs/case-studies/issue-840/self-hosting).\n\nFresh real Agent CLI session `ses_067e264b6ffeHW9PeHP83oTupQ` also produced the release's current self-hosting projections:\n\n- **295/295** owned source modules round-trip byte-for-byte through the meta-language links network;\n- the focused **41-module** `agentic_coding` self-AST census records the subsystem generalized by this issue;\n- the strict branch metric is **42.11%** (**6,260/14,866** changed lines, 3/16 commits), and the projected release ratchet holds against `origin/main`.\n\nThe transcript, server trace, generated projections, and exact session-binding commit trailers are preserved under [`self-hosting-projection/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-840-6654ade0a597/docs/case-studies/issue-840/self-hosting-projection). The complete workflow is reproducible with [`experiments/issue_840_self_hosting_projection/run.sh`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-840-6654ade0a597/experiments/issue_840_self_hosting_projection/run.sh).\n\nCloses #840\n","created_at":"2026-07-24T21:21:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T08:35:25Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gist